              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did cukki mean, and what did mōḍa mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮರ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರ (mara) — \"a tree\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two syllables, and one of the oldest words the family has. Tamil says maram, Malayalam maram, and Kannada let the closing -m fall away, as it has a habit of doing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮರ (mara) is the standing tree and equally the wood it is cut into. A carpenter and a forester reach for the same word, and Kannada has felt no need to split them — the thing and the material are one item as far as the language is concerned."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the first word of this chapter for a plain reason: everything else here is a part of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The thing the next four words belong to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mara",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *mara*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "doḍḍa mara — \"a big tree\" — with the describing word in front, where Kannada keeps it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *doḍḍa mara* — \"a big tree\" — with the describing word in front, where Kannada keeps it]"
            }
          ]
