        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕೊಂಬೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೊಂಬೆ (kombe) — \"a branch\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Beside it stands ಕೊಂಬು (kombu), a horn, and the two are the same word wearing different endings. A branch is what a ಮರ (mara) has on its head, and the language saw an animal's horn and a tree's limb as one shape: something hard that grows outward and forks."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That picture is not a Kannada peculiarity. Tamil keeps kombu doing both jobs as well, so the joining is old — older than any of the four sisters."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English does the reverse trick and puts the tree onto the animal, calling the branched horns of a stag its antlers and its crown. The picture travels in whichever direction a language happens to take it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the tree, and what comes out of it sideways."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kombe",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kombe*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mara, then kombe, and say which one holds the other up",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *mara*, then *kombe*, and say which one holds the other up]"
            }
